# Scoped vulnerability suppressions.
#
# Every entry below is a transitive dependency vendored INSIDE
# @anthropic-ai/claude-code, which this image pins to the newest published
# release (2.1.222). None of them can be fixed by upgrading: there is no later
# claude-code release, and the vendored tree is not ours to patch. Suppression
# is therefore the only alternative to a permanently red pipeline.
#
# Reachability from this add-on is nil for all of them. The CLI is invoked
# once per generation with a prompt this repository constructs, and it runs
# with all built-in tools, MCP, slash commands, settings sources and session
# persistence disabled, as UID 10001, with no inbound network path. It never
# parses attacker-supplied archives, globs, or certificates on our behalf.
#
# REVIEW BY 2026-11-05. Re-check on every claude-code bump: drop any entry the
# new release fixes, and do not extend this file to cover our own dependencies.
# Anything reachable from Python code in src/ must be fixed, never ignored.

# brace-expansion - ReDoS / memory exhaustion. We pass no user-supplied brace
# patterns; glob expansion is disabled along with the file tools.
CVE-2026-13149
CVE-2026-14257
CVE-2026-69152

# ip-address - parsing of untrusted IPv4/IPv6 input. No network input is parsed;
# the add-on makes no inbound connections.
CVE-2026-69192

# picomatch - ReDoS via crafted extglob patterns. Reached only through the file
# matching tools, which are disabled on every invocation.
CVE-2026-33671

# sigstore - certificateOIDs verification ignored. Used by claude-code's own
# update-verification path, which this image never runs: the version is pinned
# at build time and the container has no self-update mechanism.
CVE-2026-48815

# tar - DoS via gzip bomb / malformed header. Used by claude-code's installer
# path, not at runtime. The image installs the package at build time from npm
# over TLS and never extracts an archive during a generation run.
CVE-2026-59873
CVE-2026-59874
